08.gbm00686 Yamada, T. and Sekiguchi, Y. (2018). Bellilinea. In Bergey's Manual of Systematics of Archaea and Bacteria (eds W. B. Whitman, F. Rainey, P. Kämpfer, M. Trujillo, J. Chun, P. DeVos, B. Hedlund and S. Dedysh). doi:10.1002/9781118960608.gbm01479 Acetonema Caldicoprobacter | Rainey, F. A. (2015). Acetonema. In Bergey's Manual of Systematics of Archaea and Bacteria (eds W. B. Whitman, F. Rainey, P. Kämpfer, M. Trujillo, J. Chun, P. DeVos, B. Hedlund and S. Dedysh). doi:10.1002/9781118960608.gbm00686 Yokoyama, H. , Wagner, I. D. and Wiegel, J. (2017). Caldicoprobacter. In Bergey's Manual of Systematics of Archaea and Bacteria (eds W. B. Whitman, F. Rainey, P. Kämpfer, M. Trujillo, J. Chun, P. DeVos, B. Hedlund and S. Dedysh). doi:10.1002/9781118960608.gbm01380 Acetonema Caldilinea | Rainey, F. A. (2015). Acetonema. In Bergey's Manual of Systematics of Archaea and Bacteria (eds W. B. Whitman, F. Rainey, P. Kämpfer, M. Trujillo, J. Chun, P. DeVos, B. Hedlund and S. Dedysh). doi:10.1002/9781118960608.gbm00686 Grégoire, P., Bohli, M., Cayol, J. L., Joseph, M., Guasco, S., Dubourg, K., Cambar, J., Michotey, V., Bonin, P., Fardeau, M. L. & Ollivier, B. (2011). Caldilinea tarbellica sp. nov., a filamentous, thermophilic, anaerobic bacterium isolated from a deep hot aquifer in the Aquitaine Basin. International journal of systematic and evolutionary microbiology, 61(6), 1436-1441. doi:10.1099/ijs.0.025676-0137--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn46view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/9781118960608.gbm00239\",\"lineno\":null}); \nURL https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/9781118960608.gbm00239 is not accessible via this tool.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n<i>Gardnerella</i><link href='#gbm00020-note-0001 #gbm00020-note-0002'></link> - Storms - Major Reference Works - Wiley Online Library (https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/9781118960608.gbm00020)\nciteturn46view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/9781118960608.gbm00020\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 309\nL0:   * [Button: Skip to Article Content]\nL1:   * [Button: Skip to Article Information]\nL2: \nL3: [Input: Search]Search within[Select]\nL4: \nL5:   * Search term[Input: Search][Input]\nL6: \nL7: 【0†Advanced Search】 【1†Citation Search】\nL8: \nL9:   * Search term[Input: Search]\nL10: \nL11: 【2†Advanced Search】 【3†Citation Search】\nL12: \nL13: Login / Register\nL14: ## Gardnerella【4†^{‡,}】【5†^{‡}】\nL15: \nL16: 【6†Virginie Storms】,\nL17: \nL18: Virginie Storms\nL19: \nL20: Lab. voor Microbiologie en Microbiele Genetica, Faculteit Wetenschappen, Univeristeit of Gent, K.L. Ledeganckstraat 35, Ghent, B-9000 Belgium\nL21: \nL22: 【6†Search for more papers by this author】\nL23: \nL24: 【7†Peter Vandamme】,\nL25: \nL26: Peter Vandamme\nL27: \nL28: Laboratorium voor Microbiologie, Faculteit Wetenschappen, Universiteit Gent, Ledeganckstraat 35, Gent, B-9000 Belgium\nL29: \nL30: 【7†Search for more papers by this author】\nL31: \nL32: 【6†Virginie Storms】,\nL33: \nL34: Virginie Storms\nL35: Lab. voor Microbiologie en Microbiele Genetica, Faculteit Wetenschappen, Univeristeit of Gent, K.L. Ledeganckstraat 35, Ghent, B-9000 Belgium\nL36: \nL37: 【6†Search for more papers by this author】\nL38: \nL39: 【7†Peter Vandamme】,\nL40: \nL41: Peter Vandamme\nL42: \nL43: Laboratorium voor Microbiologie, Faculteit Wetenschappen, Universiteit Gent, Ledeganckstraat 35, Gent, B-9000 Belgium\nL44: \nL45: 【7†Search for more papers by this author】\nL46: \nL47: First published: 14 September 2015\nL48: 【8†https://doi.org/10.1002/9781118960608.gbm00020 Digital Object Identifier (DOI)†doi.org】\nL49: \nL50: view metrics\nL51: \nL52: ^{†}\nL53: \nL54: Greenwood and Pickett 【9†1980】, 176^{VP}\nL55: \nL56: ^{‡}\nL57: \nL58: Published by John Wiley & Sons, Inc., in association with Bergey's Manual Trust.\nL59: \nL60: 【10†Read the full text】\nL61: \nL62: CITE\nL63: \nL64: 【11†Tools】\nL65: \nL66: Share full-text access\nL67: \nL68: Please review our 【12†Terms and Conditions of Use】 and check box below to share full-text version of article.\nL69: \nL70: [Input]I have read and accept the Wiley Online Library Terms and Conditions of Use\nL71: \nL72: * * *\nL73: Shareable Link\nL74: \nL75: Use the link below to share a full-text version of this article with your friends and colleagues. 【13†Learn more.】\nL76: \nL77: [Button: Copy URL]\nL78: \nL79: Share a link\nL80: \nL81: Share on\nL82: ### Abstract\nL83: \nL84: Gard.ner.el'la. N.L. fem. dim. n. Gardnerella named after H.L. Gardner.\nL85: Pleomorphic rods ~0.5 µm in diameter and 1.5–2.5 µm in length. Filaments do not occur. Neither capsules nor endospores are formed. Gram-stain-negative to Gram-stain-variable. Nonmotile. Facultatively anaerobic. Fastidious in growth requirements. Catalase- and oxidase-negative. Chemo-organotrophic, with a fermentative type of metabolism. Acid, but no gas, is produced from a variety of carbohydrates, including maltose and starch. Acetic acid is the major product of fermentation. Hippurate is hydrolyzed.\nL86: Human blood, but not sheep blood, is hemolyzed. Found in the human genital and urinary tracts.\nL87: DNA G+C content (mol%): 42–44 (Bd).\nL88: \nL89: Type species: Gardnerella vaginalis (Gardner and Dukes 1 9 5 5) Greenwood and Pickett 1 9 8 0, 176^{VP} (Haemophilus vaginalis Gardner and Dukes 1 9 5 5, 963).\nL90: ### Taxonomic and Nomenclature Notes\nL91: \nL92: According to the List of Prokaryotic names with Standing in Nomenclature (LPSN), the taxonomic status of the genus 【14†Gardnerella†lpsn.dsmz.de】 is: correct name (last update, April 2026)^{*}.\nL93: \nL94: LPSN classification: 【15†Bacteria†lpsn.dsmz.de】 / 【16†Bacillati†lpsn.dsmz.de】 / 【17†Actinomycetota†lpsn.dsmz.de】 / 【18†Actinomycetes†lpsn.dsmz.de】 / 【19†Bifidobacteriales†lpsn.dsmz.de】 / 【20†Bifidobacteriaceae†lpsn.dsmz.de】 / 【14†Gardnerella†lpsn.dsmz.de】\nL95: The genus Gardnerella can also be recovered in the Genome Taxonomy Database (GTDB) as 【21†g__Bifidobacterium†gtdb.ecogenomic.org】 (version v232)^{**}.\nL96: \nL97: GTDB classification: 【22†d__Bacteria†gtdb.ecogenomic.org】 / 【23†p__Actinomycetota†gtdb.ecogenomic.org】 / 【24†c__Actinomycetes†gtdb.ecogenomic.org】 / 【25†o__Actinomycetales†gtdb.ecogenomic.org】 / 【26†f__Bifidobacteriaceae†gtdb.ecogenomic.org】 / 【21†g__Bifidobacterium†gtdb.ecogenomic.org】\nL98: ^{*} Freese, H.M., Meier-Kolthoff, J.P., Sardà Carbasse, J., Afolayan, A.O., Göker, M. (2026). TYGS and LPSN in 2025: a Global Core Biodata Resource for genome-based classification and nomenclature of prokaryotes within DSMZ Digital Diversity. Nucleic Acids Res, 54(D1), D884–D891; doi: 【27†10.1093/nar/gkaf1110†doi.org】\nL99: ^{**} Parks, D.H., Chaumeil, P.-A., Mussig, A.J., Rinke, C., Chuvochina, M., Hugenholtz, P. (2026). GTDB release 10: a complete and systematic taxonomy for 715.230 bacterial and 17.245 archaeal genomes. Nucleic Acids Res, 54(D1), D743–D754; doi: 【28†10.1093/nar/gkaf1040†doi.org】\nL100: ##\nL101: \nL102: References\nL103: \nL104:   * Balsdon, M.J., G.E. Taylor, L. Pead and R. Maskell. 1980. Corynebacterium vaginale and vaginitis: a controlled trial of treatment. Lancet 1: 501–503.\nL105: \nL106: 【29†CAS】 【30†PubMed】 【31†Web of Science®】 【32†Google Scholar】\nL107: \nL108:   * Bradshaw, C.S., S.N. Tabrizi, C.K. Fairley, A.N. Morton, E. Rudland and S.M. Garland. 2006. The association of Atopobium vaginae and Gardnerella vaginalis with bacterial vaginosis and recurrence after oral metronidazole therapy. J. Infect. Dis. 194: 828–836.\nL109: 【33†CAS】 【34†PubMed】 【35†Web of Science®】 【36†Google Scholar】\nL110: \nL111:   * Briselden, A.M. and S.L. Hillier. 1994. Evaluation of affirm VP Microbial Identification Test for Gardnerella vaginalis and Trichomonas vaginalis. J. Clin. Microbiol. 32: 148