ements. Catalase- and oxidase-negative. Chemo-organotrophic, with a fermentative type of metabolism. Acid, but no gas, is produced from a variety of carbohydrates, including maltose and starch. Acetic acid is the major product of fermentation. Hippurate is hydrolyzed.\nL86: Human blood, but not sheep blood, is hemolyzed. Found in the human genital and urinary tracts.\nL87: DNA G+C content (mol%): 42–44 (Bd).\nL88: \nL89: Type species: Gardnerella vaginalis (Gardner and Dukes 1 9 5 5) Greenwood and Pickett 1 9 8 0, 176^{VP} (Haemophilus vaginalis Gardner and Dukes 1 9 5 5, 963).\nL90: ### Taxonomic and Nomenclature Notes\nL91: \nL92: According to the List of Prokaryotic names with Standing in Nomenclature (LPSN), the taxonomic status of the genus 【14†Gardnerella†lpsn.dsmz.de】 is: correct name (last update, April 2026)^{*}.\nL93: \nL94: LPSN classification: 【15†Bacteria†lpsn.dsmz.de】 / 【16†Bacillati†lpsn.dsmz.de】 / 【17†Actinomycetota†lpsn.dsmz.de】 / 【18†Actinomycetes†lpsn.dsmz.de】 / 【19†Bifidobacteriales†lpsn.dsmz.de】 / 【20†Bifidobacteriaceae†lpsn.dsmz.de】 / 【14†Gardnerella†lpsn.dsmz.de】\nL95: The genus Gardnerella can also be recovered in the Genome Taxonomy Database (GTDB) as 【21†g__Bifidobacterium†gtdb.ecogenomic.org】 (version v232)^{**}.\nL96: \nL97: GTDB classification: 【22†d__Bacteria†gtdb.ecogenomic.org】 / 【23†p__Actinomycetota†gtdb.ecogenomic.org】 / 【24†c__Actinomycetes†gtdb.ecogenomic.org】 / 【25†o__Actinomycetales†gtdb.ecogenomic.org】 / 【26†f__Bifidobacteriaceae†gtdb.ecogenomic.org】 / 【21†g__Bifidobacterium†gtdb.ecogenomic.org】\nL98: ^{*} Freese, H.M., Meier-Kolthoff, J.P., Sardà Carbasse, J., Afolayan, A.O., Göker, M. (2026). TYGS and LPSN in 2025: a Global Core Biodata Resource for genome-based classification and nomenclature of prokaryotes within DSMZ Digital Diversity. Nucleic Acids Res, 54(D1), D884–D891; doi: 【27†10.1093/nar/gkaf1110†doi.org】\nL99: ^{**} Parks, D.H., Chaumeil, P.-A., Mussig, A.J., Rinke, C., Chuvochina, M., Hugenholtz, P. (2026). GTDB r